1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,760
We are now at the exact point where the sea meets the river,

2
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:09,280
one of the most significant moments on the entire route through the Grotta del Buemirino.

3
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:13,760
If you look down beneath you, you will notice a small difference in level,

4
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:17,520
a natural rocky step just a few centimeters high,

5
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:20,400
but enough to separate two different worlds.

6
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:23,920
In the lower level is salt water coming from the sea,

7
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:29,040
in the slightly higher level is fresh water, fed by the underground river.

8
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:31,840
During the summer months, when rainfall is scarce,

9
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:35,840
the river significantly reduces its flow and tends to stagnate.

10
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:40,320
In these conditions, the two bodies of water remain separate,

11
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:43,120
maintaining an almost motionless equilibrium.

12
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:48,800
During the winter months, on the other hand, the river is fed once again by rain.

13
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:53,760
The flow increases and, already in the low season, if you are lucky,

14
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:58,800
it is right here at this spot that you may observe a small waterfall of fresh water.

15
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:03,680
Pouring down towards the sea level, it is a particularly evocative moment.

16
00:01:04,240 --> 00:01:07,760
Before our very eyes, the process that over millennia

17
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:12,400
has contributed to the formation of these cavities is made clearly visible.

18
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:16,160
Here we are not merely witnessing the meeting of two bodies of water,

19
00:01:16,160 --> 00:01:19,760
but the meeting of two forces, the marine and the fluvial.

20
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:23,360
It is a dynamic equilibrium which varies with the seasons

21
00:01:23,360 --> 00:01:28,000
and which continues, even today, to slowly shape the interior of the mountain.

